@startuml qnx_dispatch_server_notify_activity
title QnxDispatchServer - notification admission

start
:Enter Notify(message) on its caller's thread;
if (Message exceeds max_notify_size_?) then (yes)
    :Return EMSGSIZE;
    stop
else (within bound)
    :Lock send_mutex_;
endif
if (Message is empty and a ping event is active?) then (yes)
    :Recover server and MsgDeliverEvent(rcvid_, ping_event_)\nIgnore the result;
    :Unlock and return success without queueing;
    stop
else (queued notification)
    :Inspect notify_pool_;
endif
if (No free notification record?) then (yes)
    :Unlock and return ENOBUFS;
    stop
else (record available)
    :Pop a record from notify_pool_;
endif
:Copy payload into the record and append it to send_queue_;
if (A select event is active?) then (yes)
    :Recover server and MsgDeliverEvent(rcvid_, select_event_)\nIgnore the result;
else (not registered)
    :Keep the record queued without a wakeup;
endif
:Unlock and return success;
stop

legend
    An active ping bypasses the FIFO and consumes no notification record.
    Before event registration, queued notification admission needs no OCB lookup.
    A later engine event-registration handler can announce already-queued data.
    The queue mutex remains held through native event delivery.
    Success is local admission/attempted signaling, not confirmed receipt.
endlegend

@enduml
